Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 16:29:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Carry the Terms in the app, and point Privacy at mebs.app

The Terms of Use row opened https://mbanguraproject-ai.github.io/terms/,
which was never published and returned a 404. That is the one screen a
Play reviewer is most likely to open, and the user most likely to open
after something goes wrong.

Terms now live in the binary rather than behind a link. They cannot rot,
they work with no connection - which is how most of this app is used -
and they ship and version with the build they describe. Fourteen clauses
covering the licence, eligibility, ownership of the user's own files,
acceptable use, Plus billing through Google Play, advertising and the
EEA consent form, the Google components the app builds on, warranty
disclaimers, liability limits, termination and governing law.

The warranty clause says plainly that Morpho is a tool and not
professional advice, and singles out the cases where that bites: invoices,
receipts, signed and stamped PDFs, Bates sets, and redaction. Someone who
redacts a document and ships it should have been told to check it first.

Privacy Policy now points at https://mebs.app/privacy/morpho, verified
serving a real policy rather than assumed.

Version 1.0.9 (10). Nothing else changed: no file under ads/, review/ or
PdfIo.kt is touched, and the signing config is intact.

